From: PocketGo S30 CFW
Subject: [PATCH] splash: initialize the display without a splash image

With stdout/stderr on serial only (patch 0002) and
SYS_CONSOLE_IS_IN_ENV, U-Boot probes the video device only in
bmp_display(), from splash_display(). When the splash image can't be
loaded (no SD card: SPI flash boot, or FEL with the card out),
splash_display() returns before that, and the display is never set up.
Linux boots with panel_ilitek_ili9488_dsi.handoff=1, which skips the
panel init, so the screen stays black (vblank waits time out). Probe the
video device on that path too.

--- a/common/splash.c
+++ b/common/splash.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <display_options.h>
+#include <dm.h>
 #include <env.h>
 #include <splash.h>
 #include <video.h>
@@ -171,8 +172,19 @@
 
 	addr = hextoul(s, NULL);
 	ret = splash_screen_prepare();
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		struct udevice *dev;
+
+		/*
+		 * No image (e.g. no SD card for splashsource=mmc_fs). With the
+		 * console off the display, drawing the splash is the only thing
+		 * that probes it: bring it up anyway, blank, so the OS finds an
+		 * initialized panel.
+		 */
+		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_VIDEO))
+			uclass_first_device(UCLASS_VIDEO, &dev);
 		return ret;
+	}
 
 	splash_get_pos(&x, &y);
 
